From 3f0765cba5537afe30e280e5bdba30c76cb1f1f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 20:03:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 265/265] BML: report effective primary/guest traffic
 separation VLAN IDs

Add db::get_traffic_separation_primary_vid()/get_traffic_separation_guest_vid()
to resolve the effective VLAN IDs for an agent from, in order: an explicit
Default 802.1Q setting, a per-SSID traffic separation policy (matched by
vap_type), or the controller's configured PrivateVID/GuestVID fallback
used for custom traffic separation.

Report these on BML_NODE.gw_ire (primary_vlan_id/guest_vlan_id) instead of
the old per-VAP vlan_id, since the VLAN assignment is per-bridge (private/
guest), not per individual VAP, matching the 8021q-subifaces traffic
separation design. beerocks_cli_bml now prints a per-agent "Traffic
separation:" summary line with these two VLAN IDs.

get_traffic_separation_guest_vid()'s configured-GuestVID fallback path now
validates the value against the same [1, 4094] VLAN ID range as
get_traffic_separation_primary_vid()'s PrivateVID fallback, returning 0
(not set) on an out-of-range value instead of silently truncating it via
the uint16_t cast.

Signed-off-by: Stephan Raj Ignatious Durairaj <signatio@qti.qualcomm.com>
